<h2>Three tiny steps to start</h2>
<p class="sub">No maths needed. If you can spot a missing number, you can play Sudoku.</p>
<div class="steps">
<a class="step" href="https://sudokubunny.com/"><div class="n">1</div><h3>Pick a size</h3><p>4x4 for beginners, 6x6 for warm-ups and 9x9 when you feel ready.</p></a>
<a class="step" href="https://sudokubunny.com/sudoku-solver/"><div class="n">2</div><h3>Stuck? Peek!</h3><p>The solver and smart hints explain each move in plain words.</p></a>
<a class="step" href="https://sudokubunny.com/printable-sudoku/"><div class="n">3</div><h3>Print and share</h3><p>Make a puzzle pack for class, car rides or grandparents.</p></a>
</div>
</div>

<div class="blk">
<h2>Try one right here</h2>
<p class="sub">A mini 4x4 example. Every row, column and 2x2 box needs the digits 1 to 4 exactly once.</p>
<div class="demo">
<div class="board" aria-label="Example 4 by 4 sudoku board">
<div class="g">1</div><div class="q">?</div><div class="g">3</div><div class="g">4</div>
<div class="g">3</div><div class="g">4</div><div class="g">1</div><div class="g">2</div>
<div class="g">2</div><div class="g">1</div><div class="g">4</div><div class="g">3</div>
<div class="g">4</div><div class="g">3</div><div class="g">2</div><div class="g">1</div>
</div>
<div>
<h3>Can you spot the missing number?</h3>
<p>Look at the top row: it already has 1, 3 and 4, so the yellow square can only be a 2.</p>
<p>That is the whole secret of Sudoku. You are not guessing, you are ruling things out. Bigger boards simply repeat the idea more times.</p>
<a class="btn" href="https://sudokubunny.com/">Play a real 4x4</a>
</div>
</div>
</div>

